 To apply a Gaussian filter before the Sobel edge detection in MATLAB, you need to add an extra step to your existing code. Here's how you can modify it:
```matlab
% Read input image and convert to grayscale
input_image = imread('image.jpg');
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);
% Apply Gaussian filter
gaussian_filter = fspecial('gaussian', [3 3], 0.5); % Standard deviation can be adjusted
filtered_image = imfilter(gray_image, gaussian_filter, 'same');
% Define Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
% Apply Sobel operator in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');
% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');
% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);
% Display original image, filtered image, and edge image
subplot(1,3,1), imshow(input_image), title('Original Image');
subplot(1,3,2), imshow(filtered_image), title('Filtered Image');
subplot(1,3,3), imshow(edge_image), title('Edge Image');
```
In this modified code, we first apply a Gaussian filter using `imfilter()` function with a standard deviation of 0.5 (you can adjust this value as per your requirement). The rest of the code remains the same as before. This modification helps in reducing the noise present in the image before detecting the edges using the Sobel operator.

